  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Johnny Roberts Memorial is one of Colorado's oldest courses — a John Bird design from 1978 that was given a 'Back to the Future' redesign into the short, technical gem it is today. From the standard pins it plays 3,547 feet at par 54, with mature trees turning every hole into a putter-and-midrange puzzle.",
    "It's the kind of course that does two jobs at once: forgiving enough to teach a beginner their lines, and technical enough that experienced players use it to sharpen their accuracy. Free to play with concrete tees, Mach 5 baskets, restrooms, and easy cart access near Olde Town Arvada.",
    "Nearly 10,000 players have rated it — the definition of a local institution."
  ],
